# Private deny-list — NEVER COMMIT THIS FILE
#
# Literal identifiers that cannot be recognised by shape: GCP project ids, hosted
# zone names, bucket names that look like ordinary slugs, internal hostnames.
#
# `tests/test_no_private_leakage.py` reads this file when it exists and fails if
# any value appears anywhere in the tree. When the file is absent (as it is in
# the published repo) that check is skipped and only the shape rules run.
#
# This indirection exists because the alternative -- listing real identifiers in
# the published test -- would leak exactly what the test is meant to protect.
#
# One value per line. `#` starts a comment. Matching is plain substring, so keep
# entries specific enough to avoid false positives.
#
# Example entries (these are placeholders, replace with real values):
#
#   my-gcp-project-id
#   my-art-bucket-name
#   internal-hostname.example.internal
